From d9d2bd2a8530a220aaf45551ddd45b7ae9f30a67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RivonClaw CI <ci@rivonclaw.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 03:26:12 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] vendor(openclaw): scale SQLite integrity budget with database
 size

Why:
- The pinned vendor runs the async admission/maintenance full-file integrity check in a child process with a fixed 30-second lifetime. A healthy multi-GB agent database cannot finish inside it, so the child is SIGKILLed, Gateway startup fails, Desktop restarts the Gateway, and the check starts over forever.
- Backports upstream commit a6a4e88da29863c8527bef2710f7090e3a0d95d8 (fix(sqlite): scale the integrity child budget with database size, #141918): budget = 30 s + 1 s per 32 MiB, capped at 30 minutes, with path, size, and budget in the log and timeout error.
- Also carries its prerequisite 31a823079ed837c43ac0cd85a0c46d9dcbc6750c (fix(sqlite): report observed integrity timeout phases, #141669); a6a4e88da29 does not apply without the lastObservedPhase plumbing it introduces.

Removal:
- Drop when .openclaw-version contains upstream commit a6a4e88da29863c8527bef2710f7090e3a0d95d8 (which already contains 31a823079ed837c43ac0cd85a0c46d9dcbc6750c).

Tests:
- apps/desktop/src/gateway/vendor-sqlite-integrity-budget.sentinel.test.ts
- vendor/openclaw/src/infra/sqlite-integrity.test.ts
- vendor/openclaw/src/infra/sqlite-readonly-worker.test.ts
